Implement `shared/constants.py`: the frozen vocabulary every other module imports rather than
redeclaring.

<responsibility>
Declare enums, Redis key names, table names, and the default values for tunables.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
This module DOES NOT read environment variables, apply overrides, or validate configuration.
`shared/config.py` MUST own all three, importing the `DEFAULT_*` values from here as fallbacks.
This module DOES NOT know what the deployment is actually configured to.
This module DOES NOT define status transition rules or a transition guard.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
**Physical contract** — an identifier that exists in Postgres. Renaming one on either side breaks
inserts at runtime, not at import. The enum labels and table names below are physical contract.
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Enum member values reproduce the Postgres labels in `schema.sql` **byte-for-byte**,
including case. `FeatureStatus` is uppercase; `BroadcastPhase`, `DecisionPhase`, and `BuildStatus`
are lowercase. Member names may differ in case from values.
R2 (MUST): Table-name constants reproduce the table names in `schema.sql` verbatim — note
`feature_requests` and `feature_votes`, not `features` and `votes`.
R3 (MUST): Every tunable is exposed as a `DEFAULT_`-prefixed constant, so a reader can never
mistake it for the effective runtime value.
R4 (MUST NOT): Import anything outside the standard library (`enum`, `typing`).
R5 (MUST NOT): Read environment variables, open files, or perform any I/O at import time.
R6 (MUST NOT): Expose mutable module-level state — no bare list, dict, or set.
R7 (MUST): Keep `REDIS_PENDING_PITCH` and `REDIS_PITCH_RATE` as format templates containing their
named placeholders, not pre-formatted keys.
R8 (MUST): Derive every string enum from `enum.StrEnum`, never from a `(str, Enum)` mixin. On
Python 3.12 a mixin renders `str(member)` and `f"{member}"` as `ClassName.MEMBER`, so
interpolating one into a Redis key, a query filter, or a payload silently emits
`FeatureStatus.VOTING` where Postgres expects `VOTING` — the exact byte-for-byte break R1 exists
to prevent, and one that reads correctly at every call site.
R9 (MUST): Guarantee `str(member) == member.value` and `f"{member}" == member.value` for all six
enums, so a member is substitutable for its wire string anywhere without an explicit `.value`.
R10 (MUST): Expose the screening model id, temperature, request timeout, and attempt cap as `DEFAULT_`-prefixed constants so `shared/config.py` has a fallback for each. The values are a starting point for one deployment, not a fixed property of the system — every one is overridable by environment.
</contract_rules>

Legality of a status change is enforced where the change is made, not here.

`DecisionPhase` is the `decision_log.phase` column. `DecisionType` is the classification recorded
*inside* the `decision_log.decision` JSON payload (US-12) and is not a Postgres enum — the two are
different axes and MUST NOT be merged.

`RejectionReason` covers every way a pitch resolves without becoming its own public row, including
`merged`, which is a dedup outcome rather than a rejection (US-03). It travels on the Redis
`screening_results` channel and never reaches Postgres.

